    "q-81475": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81475",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal.",
      "worked_solution": "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\},$ $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\},$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{4\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{a}_{1}=-\\frac{24}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{4\\cdot 3+6\\cdot (-5)+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{35}{35}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{4\\cdot 11+6\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot (-8)}{{11}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{210}{210}[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
