    "q-140358": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140358",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal.",
      "worked_solution": "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 1+5\\cdot (-1)}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{1}=-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{3\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1}{(-3)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
